#
# Conformance case: teleology/conjunctive-vs-disjunctive (issue #1055 W1, Task 5).
#
# A conjunctive goal and a disjunctive goal over the SAME two atomic sub-targets,
# where exactly one sub-target's situation obtains. The native teleology evaluator
# (teleology_lowering) evaluates both goals over the world's logic:Path and emits a
# factored logic:GoalEvaluation each:
#   * the conjunctive goal needs ALL operands  → Unsatisfied + Completed (no edge);
#   * the disjunctive goal needs ANY operand   → Satisfied  + Completed (→ bridged
#     flat gmeow:satisfiedBy edge under the default vantage).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the program axioms the projections need (a minimal,
# clean-compiling, certifiable positive declaration — no asserted teleology triples
# here, exactly as the foundation cases keep their world facts in input.nq).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/conjunctive-vs-disjunctive/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
